Subject: binutils: fix AC_CHECK_FUNCS link test so it is not folded away by -flto

Autoconf's AC_CHECK_FUNCS test compares a global function pointer to
the function itself ("return f != FUNC;").  Under -flto that comparison
is constant-folded and the reference to FUNC is dropped, so the test
passes even when the function is absent, giving false HAVE_* results
(e.g. for fprintf_unlocked, which glibc lacks).  Override
AC_LANG_FUNC_LINK_TRY(C) in aclocal.m4 to call the function, as later
Autoconf releases do, and update the generated tests in configure to
match, for bfd, gas, gprof and opcodes.
---
--- a/bfd/configure
+++ b/bfd/configure
@@ -6221,8 +6221,6 @@
     something starting with __ and the normal name is an alias.  */
 #if defined (__stub_$ac_func) || defined (__stub___$ac_func)
 choke me
-#else
-char (*f) () = $ac_func;
 #endif
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
@@ -6231,7 +6229,7 @@
 int
 main ()
 {
-return f != $ac_func;
+return $ac_func ();
   ;
   return 0;
 }
